        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Well, there is neovim/neovim#39827, but I am not sure it is even related (as I can not reproduce the error from the test fail).\r\n\r\n**Edit**: Yes, it is an upstream issue, technically speaking. In this case there is an extra [`BufEnter` event triggered](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39827#issuecomment-4470869254), which arguably should not happen. This triggers [directory tracking callback](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/18797ed18f347d0d0da27fec28a67979b1207f70/lua/mini/files.lua#L1383) which [deletes a buffer before the \"original\" `nvim_buf_delete()` can](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/18797ed18f347d0d0da27fec28a67979b1207f70/lua/mini/files.lua#L1434). Hence the error.\r\n\r\nLet's wait a bit for this to be resolved upstream. Otherwise, moving those cleanup commands after `MiniFiles.close()` looks fine, but I'd use `pcall(child.api.nvim_buf_delete, ...)` instead of an extra `if` check.",
