            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup()\r\nrequire('mini.pick').setup()\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. nvim\r\n2. `:lua MiniPick.default_choose('/home/user/somedir')`\r\n3. `:lua vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(1, { force = true })`\r\n4. Observe: \r\n\r\n```lua\r\nE5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: Failed to unload buffer.                                                                                                                                        \r\nstack traceback:                                                                                                                                                                               \r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_buf_delete'                                                                                                                                                     \r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk    \r\n```\r\n\r\nNote:\r\nSucceeds when step one takes an argument: `nvim somefile.txt`\r\nAlso succeeds when replacing step 2 with: `lua MiniFiles.open('/home/user/somedir')`",
